{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/406618-max-roman-and-colorado-rockies-protectorate-failure","id":406618,"title":"Max Roman and Colorado Rockies Protectorate failure","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-02-15T06:31:30-08:00","id":406618,"title":"Max Roman and Colorado Rockies Protectorate failure","content":"<a href=\"http://www.takepart.com/article/2015/02/12/grand-canyon-wolf-dead\" target=\"_blank\">First wolf seen from over 70 years in Colorado is killed by hunters</a>. When I look over this news, it fills my Uratha part of heart with sorrow. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> It also lead to question - if Colorado is infamous from the no wolf sightings in over seven decades, does not one of greatest Protectorates in 1ed books a bit improbable? If wolves are sight of the past in area, how werewolves can be so common in there? Would not humans suspect something when someone would see packs in Urhan forms roaming the streets and deserts, and then discover the wolves at large have not moved to area? Not too mention the Urshul form would be <b>very</b> much odd thing to see in this Territories.<br /> <br /> Also, in WoD the <i>Echo</i> she-wolf from the article could be one of <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/ephemera-werewolf-the-forsaken/\" target=\"_blank\">Urhanu</a>, wolf-born Uratha, that was trying to reclaim the land for her future pack of wolves to repopulate it. But this idea sounds to me a bit cWoD-like in mine head.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-15T06:59:48-08:00","id":406672,"title":"","content":"You could equally ask that question of lots of places. I mean, there aren't too many wolfs running round Bristol, and yet it's going to be a setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-15T06:59:49-08:00","id":406673,"title":"","content":"Americans in general are blatantly ignorant on matters like that. The wolf shot was mistaken for a coyote (lies I belive). The wolf born is a thing in nighthorrors too though do you aren't completely wrong lol","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-15T09:00:59-08:00","id":406738,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">I grew up in Colorado and currently running a W20 game set in Colorado. One of the resources I used was <b>Hunting Grounds: Rockies </b>for my game. I changed some things obviously but I read the book in detail. The whole wolves being slaughtered storyline is a big part for my Garou and there is more to it than that. But for Forsaken I think they hint there is but up to the Storyteller to work it out. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">I know what the book says, but having grown up in Colorado there is more to it and the argument and conservation of the wolves than what was covered. You can find a lot of information online. </span><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">In Colorado it is a bit strange about the wolf. Surrounding states have ran reintroducing wolves into the wild or already have wolves protected. The wolf that was killed the rancher thought was a coyote is believed to have come from one of those reintroduction programs or from New Mexico. The whole fact that the wolf seems non existent in Colorado is in itself a bit of a surprise. <br /> <br /> Now what the book fails to mention are groups like this is the Colorado Wolf and Wildlife Center in Divide, CO their website is here <a href=\"http://www.wolfeducation.org/\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.wolfeducation.org/</a> which is just something you can find with a little research. </span></span><span style=\"font-size:14px\">This is just an hour drive from Colorado Springs, I visited there when we were visiting the in laws this summer.</span><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"> Although the book is a great setting, I never just use the source book as the only information going on many times the writer misses things, makes mistakes or as time passes things get out of date. I do check out a few sites as well. Take it from a local it missing a lot on this. <br /> <br /> One can easily say that Max Roman and the </span><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Colorado Rockies Protectorate</span> may not have saved that one wolf, but are working hard at educating the people of Colorado on wolves this is something my Sept has been doing for some time now. <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>ADDING Not Related</b><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Hunting Grounds: </b><b>Rockies</b> is a great setting and it is better use of Colorado and Denver than <b>Alien Hunger</b> but it does have its flaws in a lot of areas. It skips over a lot of history that you can use for Colorado that would work great for your game. I would recommend getting <b>Werewolf Wyld West</b> although W20 it covers some parts of Colorado History that should have been mentioned in the book. <br /> <br /> There are a lot of haunted houses in Denver alone. Ghosts from those that died from TB that can also be found in Boulder and Colorado Springs. The Forsaken deal with a lot of spirits so this is something to look into for a ST. </span><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4949-nene-richards","name":"Nene Richards","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4949_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-15T09:47:04-08:00","id":406794,"title":"","content":"Two things.<br /> <br /> 1) The World of Darkness is based on the real world up to certain degrees, but it's fudged on the egdes. Wolf extinction is still a thing as a global problem in WoD, but WoD's Colorado has had better conservationalists (Which would make a ton of sense given the protectorate)...unless, of course, you want to run with what the real world has said on the matter, which can lead to it's own stories.In short, it's up to you to decide which facts carry over.<br /> <br /> 2) I get the rancher's problem, but I'm still quite angry now. Our lands need wolves badly to help direct the ecosystem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 02-15-2015, 12:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-15T10:09:15-08:00","id":406803,"title":"","content":"Fun fact. The ranchers in Idaho? Who vied for wolf hunts? They're complaining about an over abundance of elk eating their crops.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-15T10:33:51-08:00","id":406821,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/406618-max-roman-and-colorado-rockies-protectorate-failure?p=406803#post406803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fun fact. The ranchers in Idaho? Who vied for wolf hunts? They're complaining about an over abundance of elk eating their crops.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have an intense amount of vitriol for Idaho, and the fact they were the first state in years to put up wolf bounties certainly didn't help.<br /> <br /> So all I can do to that is laugh my ass off and call them mean things off forum.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-15T10:36:09-08:00","id":406822,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/406618-max-roman-and-colorado-rockies-protectorate-failure#post406618\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It also lead to question - if Colorado is infamous from the no wolf sightings in over seven decades, does not one of greatest Protectorates in 1ed books a bit improbable? If wolves are sight of the past in area, how werewolves can be so common in there?</div> </div> </div> </div>For one thing, the Rockies stretch from Canada to New Mexico, Colorado being just one of the five or six states they pass through. For another, absolutely nothing says a werewolf ever has to take urhan or even near wolf-form. When they do, Lunacy or the Oath of the Moon can help assure that they won't be seen. And wolf population has nothing to do with werewolf population.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-15T12:39:55-08:00","id":406888,"title":"","content":"Yep, Lunacy can make a witness say, &quot;That was one mean big dog.&quot; Because everyone knows that it couldn't be a wolf.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/406618-max-roman-and-colorado-rockies-protectorate-failure?p=406821#post406821\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have an intense amount of vitriol for Idaho, and the fact they were the first state in years to put up wolf bounties certainly didn't help.<br /> <br /> So all I can do to that is laugh my ass off and call them mean things off forum.</div> </div> </div> </div>I forget which year it was exactly, but in one year Idaho handed out thousands of licenses to hunt wolves. Only 3 were actually taken, and those by people who weren't actively looking for them. <i>American Hunter </i>reported in a recent issue that traps are nearly useless against them. These are VERY smart, savvy animals we're talking about here. Don't count them out just yet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/233-daydreamer","name":"Daydreamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"193"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-15T13:37:44-08:00","id":406950,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Daydreamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/406618-max-roman-and-colorado-rockies-protectorate-failure?p=406888#post406888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yep, Lunacy can make a witness say, &amp;quot;That was one mean big dog.&amp;quot; Because everyone knows that it couldn't be a wolf.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I forget which year it was exactly, but in one year Idaho handed out thousands of licenses to hunt wolves. Only 3 were actually taken, and those by people who weren't actively looking for them. <i>American Hunter </i>reported in a recent issue that traps are nearly useless against them. These are VERY smart, savvy animals we're talking about here. Don't count them out just yet.</div> </div> </div> </div>I never was-the same article that informed me about Idaho's bullshit talked a little about the lack of initial response, and while I'm pleased to hear about how the wolves are outsmarting humanity, I'm not surprised. Wolves have been our major competitors for food and land for ages, they haven't done that by being simple minded creatures.<br /> <br /> If anything, I just enjoy being able to call out the stupid fucks of Idaho for being stupid fucks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-17T04:54:44-08:00","id":408792,"title":"","content":"A Protectorate's presence doesn't have anything to do with whether there are local wolf populations; let's face it, even if there <i>was</i> a native wolf population, it wouldn't exactly be a very good cover for werewolves in the middle of a densely packed urban environment, for example.<br /> <br /> Werewolves appear everywhere that humans do, regardless of what canine creatures there may be. The Uratha do have tools in their armoury to help deal with that, but to a certain extent it's just a thing that werewolves have to cope with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-17T06:18:18-08:00","id":408889,"title":"","content":"There may come a time where the only wolves on this Earth are those which walk like man.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-17T09:05:37-08:00","id":409028,"title":"","content":"Stealing inspiration from wolfen are we? (Good movie)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-17T11:34:48-08:00","id":409152,"title":"","content":"I'm just gonna leaves this link to the Center for biological diversity here. They're doing a lot to protect wolves, so I figured you guys might want to help out given the subject. Linking to their donate page doesn't work right for some reason. If you do donate, just say you want it to help wolves in the comment box.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-17T13:40:09-08:00","id":409275,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/406618-max-roman-and-colorado-rockies-protectorate-failure?p=406803#post406803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fun fact. The ranchers in Idaho? Who vied for wolf hunts? They're complaining about an over abundance of elk eating their crops.</div> </div> </div> </div>Makes sense of you look it amorally.<br /> <br /> Wolves scare the cattle, scared cattle eat less and weight less. They also tend to go after the older/sicker of the herds which could've been sold. So the solution is to remove the wolves again.<br /> <br /> Elk, same issue. Elk/Deer consume the same resources that cattle do and if there are more Elk/Deer around, there are less for cattle.<br /> <br /> For Ranchers, the solution becomes clear cut: Blast both species out of the picture to increase the profit yields from the cattle.<br /> <br /> Of course, down here in Texas, we've tried to blast feral hogs all the time. The problem is you just end up with smarter hogs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-19T23:17:21-08:00","id":412459,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/406618-max-roman-and-colorado-rockies-protectorate-failure?p=409275#post409275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem is you just end up with smarter hogs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ow. And pigs are plenty smart to start with.<br /> <br /> There are problems like that here too, wild boars are a bit of a nuisance.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}